-- Tests of Histadrut HaMorim's wage agreement of 11.5.93
-- (l4/agreements/teachers-general/1993-05-11_histadrut-hamorim_wage-agreement-1993.l4):
-- the agreement held against the takanon sections that carry its rules on.
-- They sit beside it and not in it (the client, 2026-10-22: "assertions
-- about a file should sit next to it, not be included in it");
-- agreements/teachers-general has no family root yet (MMS-548).
--
-- THE ROUND: the agreement is the first of the 1993–1995 round, and the
-- round's public-sector framework agreements — the supplement §34(ג)
-- promises, or failing one the engineers' — are not in the corpus, so the
-- agreement cannot be held against them here; §34(ג)'s supplement is an
-- input of the module. The agreement that carries §34(ג) out for this
-- union, of 19.9.94, is in the corpus and not yet encoded; ארגון המורים's
-- of 31.8.94 (encoded) carries out its own twin agreement of 11.5.93,
-- which the corpus does not hold, so it is not this agreement's measure
-- either.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `1993-05-11_histadrut-hamorim_wage-agreement-1993`
IMPORT `takanon-3-14`
IMPORT `takanon-3-18`
IMPORT `takanon-1-13`

§ `בדיקות ההסכם הקיבוצי מיום 11.5.93 (הסתדרות המורים)`

§§ `מול סעיף 3.14.3 לתקנון`

-- §3.14.3 (its source: this agreement and the committee of 25.10.93) is
-- §19(א) in the takanon's words: the 4%, the quota of 250 in 5754 and 500
-- over 5754–5755, and the same hours condition read the same way
-- (F-3.14-a, F-hh-1993-c). Over a grid of schools, the two say the same.
#ASSERT `allowance rate of a coordinator appointed on the district manager's recommendation` EQUALS `the 1993 subject coordinator's rate`

`the quota counts checked, for 1993` MEANS LIST 0, 200, 250, 251, 300, 500

#ASSERT all (GIVEN a YIELD all (GIVEN b YIELD `within the quota of district coordinators` a b EQUALS `within the 1993 quota of subject coordinators` a b)
                                `the quota counts checked, for 1993`)
            `the quota counts checked, for 1993`

GIVEN small IS A BOOLEAN, teachers IS A NUMBER, positions IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§3.14.3 and §19(א) of 1993 agree on` small teachers positions IF
    `the district manager may recommend a coordinator` `the takanon's school`
        EQUALS `a 1993 subject coordinator is appointed in` `the agreement's school`
    WHERE
        `the takanon's school` MEANS
            `district coordination case` WITH
                `average parallel classes per grade` IS (IF small THEN 1 ELSE 3)
                `entitled to subject coordination under the existing criteria` IS TRUE
                `teachers teaching the subject` IS teachers
                `positions all those teachers hold in the subject` IS positions
        `the agreement's school` MEANS
            `1993 coordination case` WITH
                `an institution with few classes, for 1993` IS small
                `teachers of the subject, for 1993` IS teachers
                `positions all the subject's teachers hold, for 1993` IS positions

#ASSERT all (GIVEN small YIELD
                all (GIVEN teachers YIELD
                        all (GIVEN positions YIELD `§3.14.3 and §19(א) of 1993 agree on` small teachers positions)
                            (LIST 0.5, 0.99, 1, 1.5))
                    (LIST 1, 2, 3))
            (LIST TRUE, FALSE)

§§ `מול סעיף 3.18 לתקנון`

-- §3.18 (its source: this agreement) is §21: the clothing supplement of a
-- crafts, art or home-economics teacher in grades 7–8 of a primary school
-- is the junior high school's for the subject; for every subject and an
-- amount, the takanon pays what §21 gives, and nothing where §21 gives
-- none.
GIVEN s IS A `subject of section 3.18`
GIVETH A `1993 clothing subject`
DECIDE `the 1993 subject for` s IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `crafts and technology` THEN `crafts and technology, for 1993`
    WHEN `art` THEN `art, for 1993`
    WHEN `home economics` THEN `home economics, for 1993`
    WHEN `another subject` THEN `another subject, for 1993`

GIVEN s IS A `subject of section 3.18`, `in grades 7–8` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§3.18 pays what §21 of 1993 gives` s `in grades 7–8` IF
    `clothing supplement in grades 7-8 of a primary school` `the takanon's teacher` EQUALS `what §21 gives`
    WHERE
        `the takanon's teacher` MEANS
            `grade 7-8 teacher` WITH
                `subject taught` IS s
                `teaches grades 7-8 in a primary school` IS `in grades 7–8`
                `the middle-school supplement for the subject` IS 500
        `what §21 gives` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the 1993 clothing supplement of a grade 7–8 teacher` (`the 1993 subject for` s) `in grades 7–8` 500
            WHEN JUST x THEN x
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

#ASSERT all (GIVEN s YIELD `§3.18 pays what §21 of 1993 gives` s TRUE AND `§3.18 pays what §21 of 1993 gives` s FALSE)
            (LIST `crafts and technology`, `art`, `home economics`, `another subject`)

§§ `מול סעיף 1.13 לתקנון — כרטיס בעמוד המקורות הסותרים`

-- §1.13.1 ¶10 (its source among others: this agreement "and the
-- clarification of the director of the conditions-of-service department",
-- which the corpus does not hold) gives the 10% from 1.9.93 to a
-- mother-teacher working "מעל 79% משרה" at the employer's demand, so long
-- as her salary with it is not above 150% of a position. §17 gives it to
-- one working "מעל ל-90% משרה (עד 140%)". The takanon pays a mother at 85%
-- of a position the agreement does not; the agreement prevails (the
-- takanon's own terms): the card "takanon-1993-mother" on מקורות סותרים.
-- (F-1.13-a, the takanon's own "79% לפחות" against "מעל 79%", is the
-- takanon's and unchanged.)
`the takanon pays the 10% from 1.9.93 at 85% of a position, where §17 of 11.5.93 asks above 90%` MEANS
        `is above 79%, as the clause of 1.9.93 words it` 0.85
    AND NOT `owed the 1993 mother-teacher supplement` TRUE 0.85 TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1993)
    AND `the 1993 mother-teacher supplement rate` EQUALS `the mother supplement rate`
#ASSERT `the takanon pays the 10% from 1.9.93 at 85% of a position, where §17 of 11.5.93 asks above 90%`

-- The two agree on the rate, and from 90% up to 136% of a position, where
-- the takanon's 150% salary cap is not reached, on the threshold too.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN p YIELD `is above 79%, as the clause of 1.9.93 words it` p
                            EQUALS `owed the 1993 mother-teacher supplement` TRUE p TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1993))
            (LIST 0.5, 0.75, 0.91, 1, 1.2, 1.36)
